From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 06:16:31 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 02/49] hjviewer: headless end-to-end test commands behind the
 hjv-e2e feature

With --features hjv-e2e (never in release builds) the app takes:
  --hjv-e2e-set-password <password>      set the permanent password, print the ID
  --hjv-e2e-forward <id> <password> <local port> <remote host> <remote port>
  --hjv-e2e-screenshot <id> <password> <out.ppm>
  --hjv-e2e-stream <id> <password> <seconds>   (video bitrate)
The controlling side logs in through the configured server like the UI
does, through the client's own Interface helpers, and reports whether the
session went direct (WebRTC) or through the relay. tools/e2e/firewall-e2e.sh
in hjviewer drives them across network namespaces whose firewalls only let
HTTPS to the server out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
